go 1.25.0

// go.work is committed on purpose. The three modules in this repository
// depend on each other (transport/web -> core and examples -> transport/web ->
// core), and none is published yet. Without a workspace, neither transport/web
// nor examples can resolve core -- `go build ./...` in transport/web fails.
// The alternative, a local `replace` in each sub-module, is exactly what must
// not happen: a replace directive travels with the published module and would
// break every downstream consumer, and it would also hide the one property
// these modules have to keep proving, that they resolve as ordinary tagged
// dependencies. Once core and transport/web are tagged this file stops being
// load-bearing and becomes a convenience for local development.
use (
	.
	./examples
	./transport/web
)
